<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51588" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">zygĭa</span></b> , ae,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζυγία</span> (prop. an
			adj. from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζύγιος</span>,
		belonging to or fit for yokes). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A tree</i>, <i>called also</i>
			carpinus, <i>horn-beam</i>: Carpinus betulus, Linn.;
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				16, 15, 26, § 67</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Zygia tibia, <i>a
				nuptial</i> or <i>marriage flute</i>,
					<i><span class="en">App. M. 4, p. 157, 37</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
